Track 1: Raw Linen Bites the Circuit
- Story & Context: In an iron-scrap depot on the outskirts of Bab Khemis, salvage trader Tariq pried open the rusted casing of an overturned transport synth to find desert rodents had packed its capacitors with coarse wool and raw linen. When Idris hooked the machine to a sputtering generator, the short-circuiting diodes emitted an erratic, stuttering pulse that Barka instantly matched on her keyed C-flute. That unscripted grease-fire jam laid down the template for the entire movement before the power cables melted into the sand. "We pulled the copper from the sand and taught the dust to choke."
