Track 2: "Who Mended This Ribbon?"
- Story & Context: Recorded during a freezing sandstorm in an outstation tent near Erg Chebbi, Barka broke down after discovering her late father's cassette archive had been sliced up to make tape-delay loops for the drum machine. Instead of canceling the session, she taped her chipped wooden flute to an amplified contact mic and delivered an uninterrupted, venomous confession over heavy sub-bass and sour minor-ninth Rhodes chords. The room smelled of kerosene, boiling mint tea, and scorched plastic as the band tracked her weeping into the flute's embouchure hole without stopping the tape. "I tore the hem to bind the wound, but both our throats still bleed."
