Track 3: Sidechain Selvedge
- Story & Context: Across the dry basin of Chott el Djerid, local truckers still tell of the night the ensemble routed their entire rhythm section through a dying truck alternator, forcing the synth chords to violently gasp for voltage. The erratic electrical decay caused the sub-bass to violently suck the air out of the track, leaving Barka's octave-dropped flute hovering like a predatory bird over the salt crust. By sunrise, the machine had seized permanently, leaving behind this single, haunted eight-minute master tape that no emulator has ever managed to replicate. "The seam is torn, the sand moves through, nothing stays stitched to you."
